{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794311420,"nonce":"TC4Tau9TaeOl9oAEcGDJH1cr+jE=","title":"fem.eval of an integral that reads a region-attached coefficient raises on the Lagrange path","message":"A test-free integrand such as d.k * u, where k is attached per region with .attach(k=...), is integrated by the Lagrange functional with no region masks, so fem.eval raises 'the per-cell mask for region ... was not threaded into this assembly path'. The weak form with the same coefficient assembles and solves. Reproduction: two .attach-ed rects, a Poisson form with d.k, then fem.eval(d.k * u, sol).","files":null}]}